  "body": "What happens: with two setups that both follow the document's post options, a change on Setup2's Post page (`SetPostOptions`, routed by `State::route_post_options` in `crates/ui/src/state_setup_post_options.rs`) writes the DOCUMENT's options whenever Setup2 does not own its options - so Setup1's posted program changes too. Same shape as #1515 (machine and post pick), which was fixed by routing to the active setup's own mount when the document has two or more setups.\n\nExpected: a post-options change on one setup's page never changes what another setup posts; with two or more setups it becomes that setup's own options (`SetSetupPostOptions`, undoable), and the page says so by name.\n\nEvidence: `route_post_options` uses `post_options_owner()` only (own-or-document), the pre-#1515 machine law. Found while fixing #1515 (PR to follow; decision file `docs/decisions/1515-setup-own-machine-pick.md`, \"Left as is\").\n\nDone means: with Setup1 and Setup2 following the document, an options change on Setup2 leaves Setup1's options and the document's unchanged, Setup2 reads the change, undo restores both; single-setup behaviour stated and pinned; the page line names the target.\n",
